TY  - JOUR
ID  - R02863
TI  - Transformations, Inhibition and Inhibition Control Methods of Sulfur in Sludge Anaerobic Digestion: A Review
AU  - Yang, Guang
AU  - Zhang, Guangming
AU  - Zhuan, Run
AU  - Yang, Anqi
AU  - Wang, Yuanyuan
PY  - 2016
JO  - Current Organic Chemistry
VL  - 20
IS  - 26
DO  - 10.2174/1385272820666160513152913
AB  - Sulfur compounds play a significant role in low treatment efficiency, production of corrosive gases and unpleasant odors during sludge anaerobic digestion, which limits its environment and economic benefits. Better understanding of sulfur transformations, inhibitions and inhibition control methods is deemed necessary for enhancing the wider application of sludge anaerobic digestion. This review presented a detailed summary of research on the pathways and properties of sulfur transformations (dissimilation, assimilation and desulfurization), sulfur inhibitors (e.g. sulfide and sulfate reducing bacteria) and their inhibition mechanisms in sludge anaerobic digestion. The effects and mechanisms of various physical (e.g. thermal and ultrasound pretreatments), chemical (e.g. oxidative pretreatments and adding metal salts) and biological control methods (microaerobic desulfuration) on sulfur inhibition were also evaluated in sludge anaerobic digestion. Besides, a proper method was proposed to control sulfur inhibition in sludge anaerobic digestion according to existing studies.
SP  - 2780
EP  - 2789
UR  - https://doi.org/10.2174/1385272820666160513152913
